{"id":"n-20261009-vxl8fj","category":"world","display_title":"Hurricane Isaias Threatens Gulf Coast","display_title_he":"הוריקן איזאיה מאיים על חוף המפרץ","short_summary":"After an unusually quiet season suppressed by El Niño, Hurricane Isaias has intensified into a Category 2 storm, prompting evacuations and states of emergency across the US Gulf Coast.","english_level":"C1","words":462,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Hurricane_Isaias_%28MODIS_2020-08-05%29.jpg/960px-Hurricane_Isaias_%28MODIS_2020-08-05%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"MODIS Land Rapid Response Team, NASA GSFC · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hurricane_Isaias_(MODIS_2020-08-05).jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/08/hurricane-isaias-gulf-coast","title":"Millions on alert as Hurricane Isaias set to bring dangerous storm surge","published_at":"2026-10-09T01:21:04.000Z"},{"name":"Wired","domain":"wired.com","url":"https://www.wired.com/story/tropical-storm-isaias-first-atlantic-hurricane-2026","title":"Tropical Storm Isaias Set to Be First Atlantic Hurricane of 2026 Season","published_at":"2026-10-07T22:00:24.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-07T22:00:24.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-09T06:20:44.622Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The 2026 Atlantic hurricane season has been remarkably quiet, largely due to a powerful El Niño event that disrupted storm formation. Meteorologists dubbed this climate pattern \"supersized,\" as it record-warmed the tropical Pacific and altered global atmospheric winds. These high-altitude winds ripped apart developing storms in the Atlantic, while dry Saharan dust further stifled cyclone activity. Consequently, the season's accumulated cyclone energy (ACE) stood at a mere 10.8 units, compared to the historical average of nearly 102. However, this period of relative calm is coming to an abrupt end. Tropical Storm Isaias recently intensified into a Category 2 hurricane, marking the very first hurricane of the 2026 season. This exceptionally late development nearly broke a historical record set in 1905, when the season's first hurricane did not materialize until October 8.","Now, millions of residents along the United States Gulf Coast are on high alert as Hurricane Isaias approaches. According to the National Weather Service (NWS), the storm has sustained winds of 100 miles per hour (160 kilometers per hour) and is projected to make landfall late Friday or early Saturday. Officials have warned of a life-threatening storm surge, torrential rainfall, and destructive winds. Consequently, hurricane warnings have been issued from Mississippi to the Florida Panhandle, while tropical storm warnings extend further west into Louisiana.","In response to the looming threat, governors in Florida, Alabama, and Georgia have declared states of emergency. Florida Governor Ron DeSantis urged residents to execute their safety plans immediately, noting that the storm is moving rapidly. Mandatory and voluntary evacuation orders have been implemented in several low-lying coastal counties in Florida, including Escambia, Okaloosa, and Franklin. Emergency management teams are actively positioning resources, and hundreds of transportation personnel are preparing infrastructure for the storm's impact.","The impending storm has already caused widespread disruptions to daily life and regional infrastructure. Numerous school districts and university campuses, including Florida State University in Tallahassee, have announced closures. Travel plans have been severely impacted; major regional airports scheduled operational shutdowns ahead of the storm's arrival. Destin-Fort Walton Beach Airport announced it would close on Thursday night, while Pensacola Airport planned to halt commercial operations on Friday morning. Furthermore, Amtrak suspended its Mardi Gras and Crescent rail services along the Gulf Coast through the weekend.","Even areas further inland are bracing for the remnants of Isaias. The NWS warned that the storm could dump up to 15 inches of rain in localized areas, raising the risk of flash flooding and isolated tornadoes across Georgia and Alabama. Meanwhile, weather offices as far north as Tennessee, Ohio, and Pennsylvania are tracking the storm's trajectory, anticipating heavy rainfall and gusty winds over the weekend. While the 2026 hurricane season may have been historically quiet, Isaias serves as a stark reminder that it only takes one powerful storm to pose a severe threat to coastal communities."],"facts":[{"fact":"The 2026 Atlantic hurricane season was exceptionally quiet due to a strong El Niño event, which record-warmed the tropical Pacific and disrupted storm formation.","sources":[2]},{"fact":"Hurricane Isaias is the first hurricane of the 2026 Atlantic season, nearly breaking the 1905 record for the latest first hurricane on record.","sources":[2]},{"fact":"Isaias intensified into a Category 2 hurricane with sustained winds of 100 mph.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Landfall is projected for the northern Gulf Coast late Friday or early Saturday.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"States of emergency have been declared in Florida, Alabama, and Georgia, with mandatory evacuations ordered in several coastal Florida counties.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The storm is causing widespread disruptions, including school and university closures, airport shutdowns in Pensacola and Destin-Fort Walton Beach, and Amtrak service suspensions.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Atlantic","lemma":"Atlantic","pos":"name","he":"אטלנטי","name":true},{"text":"hurricane","lemma":"hurricane","pos":"noun","he":"הוריקן","name":false},{"text":"season","lemma":"season","pos":"noun","he":"עונה","name":false},{"text":"rema